From 76d88f2de0e996799b8ad4bcc63f00c8ebfca751 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 23:38:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06838/11362] ARC round-2 (codex): r11l L3 -> L4 (+1), L5
 substantially scouted

Continuation of the same-day breadth-campaign game loop. r11l solved L4
(three multicolor pieces on seven handles, each must touch its
color-matched socket, five extra dotted glyphs are real blockers/decoys --
the prior "six handles" preview guess was close, corrected to seven).
Independently re-verified: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via the fixed
resolver, all 5 confirmed reached_level=4.

L5 was substantially scouted across three explorations: two black
CARRIER pieces pick up partially-colored cargo on overlap; complementary
solid halves must be fused (orange+maroon, cyan+tan) before delivery to a
matching two-color template. The orange/maroon pair was fused and
successfully delivered; cyan/tan was fused and routed toward its target,
but the attempt ran out of L5's 60-click meter on the final delivery. No
L5 win banked -- this is meaningfully further than the "not attempted"
state the prior session left it in.

reproducible_total_levels: 135 -> 136 (verified against a fresh sum).

Of the 18 round-2 games: 14 processed and committed (2 full clears: vc33,
cn04, and lp85's terminal L8; several +1-to-+4 level-ups: sp80, m0r0, ka59,
tu93, su15, r11l; honest documented nulls: bp35, g50t, dc22, sk48, sc25,
ls20). Three games (lf52, re86, s5i5) hit the 1800s codex process timeout
with no artifact produced -- inconclusive, not a null; worth a retry with
a longer budget rather than being recorded as a dead end.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
